# LibreWolf no-gms.patch  (Android)
# Owner: LW-M4-05 ("Strip Play Integrity, Firebase and push messaging")
#
# Removes every Google Play services dependency from the Fenix APK: Firebase
# Cloud Messaging (Sync/WebPush), Play Integrity (attestation), the Play In-App
# Review API, the Google Advertising ID client, the Google OSS-licenses Gradle
# plugin, and the Play services FIDO2 backend inside GeckoView.
#
#
# WHAT WAS ACTUALLY IN THE APK BEFORE THIS PATCH (measured, not grepped)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Read out of the pre-patch APK by parsing the DEX class_defs / type_ids /
# string_ids tables of all 36 classes*.dex, and by
# `aapt2 dump xmltree --file AndroidManifest.xml` on the same file.  Two APKs
# were measured and they agree exactly on the GMS numbers:
#   * ~/lw-m2-04/out-make/apk/fenix-x86_64-debug.apk  (the LW-M2-04 build)
#   * the same tree as this patch minus this patch (LW-M4-10's combined build),
#     which is the honest before/after pair.
#
#   * 2,935 Google classes DEFINED in the dex (class_defs, not merely
#     referenced):
#         1944  Lcom/google/android/gms/     of which 933 internal/, 621 common/,
#                                            194 fido/, 48 tasks/, 41 cloudmessaging/,
#                                            23 dynamite/, 22 dynamic/, 19 signin/,
#                                            12 auth/, 9 stats/, 7 ads/, 7 base/,
#                                            4 actions/, 3 security/, 1 ads_identifier/
#          459  Lcom/google/firebase/        messaging, installations, components,
#                                            datatransport, encoders, heartbeatinfo,
#                                            iid, concurrent, platforminfo, provider
#          312  Lcom/google/android/datatransport/   Firelog, the transport
#                                            firebase-messaging logs through -- it
#                                            rides in transitively and nothing in
#                                            the source tree names it
#          220  Lcom/google/android/play/    162 core/, 54 integrity/, 2 review/,
#                                            2 corecommon/
#     The full class delta of this patch, before -> after on the same tree, is
#     -3,057 / +4 (66,699 -> 63,646 defined classes): the 2,935 above, 44 under
#     mozilla/components/lib (the two deleted AC modules), 43 under
#     org/mozilla/fenix, 20 under org/mozilla/geckoview (the WebAuthn FIDO2
#     path), 8 kotlinx/coroutines/tasks (the coroutines<->Play Tasks bridge),
#     6 javax/inject and 1 com/google/errorprone annotation class that only
#     Firebase pulled in.  The 4 additions are two synthetic lambdas for the new
#     no-op IntegrityClient and BackgroundServices' shortened observer chain, and
#     two Guava backport helpers D8 re-emitted.
#   * `./scripts/android-smoke.sh --check-no-gms` reported **4,474** on that
#     APK.  That figure is a SUM OVER THREE OVERLAPPING NEEDLES
#     ("com.google.android.gms", "com/google/android/gms",
#     "Lcom/google/android/gms"), so most strings are counted twice; the number
#     of DISTINCT dex strings containing "com.google.android.gms" or
#     "com/google/android/gms" is 2,299.  Both drop to **2** -- not 0 -- and the
#     two survivors are AndroidX constants, not a Play services artifact.  See
#     "THE TWO STRINGS THAT SURVIVE" below before treating that as a leftover.
#   * 26 google/firebase-named entities in the MERGED manifest, only ONE of
#     which (the FirebasePushService <service>) is written in Fenix's own
#     AndroidManifest.xml.  The other 25 arrive through manifest merging, which
#     is why this had to be read from the built APK:
#       <uses-permission com.google.android.gms.permission.AD_ID>     (ads-identifier AAR)
#       <uses-permission com.google.android.c2dm.permission.RECEIVE>  (firebase-messaging)
#       <service  org.mozilla.fenix.push.FirebasePushService>         (Fenix)
#                 + <action com.google.firebase.MESSAGING_EVENT>
#       <service  com.google.firebase.messaging.FirebaseMessagingService>
#       <service  com.google.firebase.components.ComponentDiscoveryService>
#                 + 6 <meta-data> ComponentRegistrar entries
#       <receiver com.google.firebase.iid.FirebaseInstanceIdReceiver>
#                 permission com.google.android.c2dm.permission.SEND
#       <provider com.google.firebase.provider.FirebaseInitProvider>
#                 authorities ${applicationId}.firebaseinitprovider
#                 -- a ContentProvider, i.e. it runs at process start, before
#                 Application.onCreate()
#       <activity com.google.android.gms.common.api.GoogleApiActivity>
#       <activity com.google.android.play.core.common.PlayCoreDialogWrapperActivity>
#       <meta-data com.google.android.gms.version>
#       <service  com.google.android.datatransport.runtime...JobInfoSchedulerService>
#       <receiver com.google.android.datatransport.runtime...AlarmManagerSchedulerBroadcastReceiver>
#       <service  com.google.android.datatransport.runtime.backends.TransportBackendDiscovery>
#       3 firebase_*_auto_init / analytics_collection <meta-data> flags
#   * NO native library and no APK entry with "gms" in its name: unlike Adjust
#     (LW-M4-02, libsigner.so) these libraries are pure Java/Kotlin.  6 non-dex
#     APK entries went away with them (firebase-*.properties, res/raw/
#     firebase_common_keep.xml).
#
#
# "ALREADY OFF" IS NOT ABSENCE -- TWICE, AND BOTH WERE CHECKED
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Two of the four Play features were already inert in a LibreWolf build, and
# neither fact removes a single class from the APK:
#
#   * PUSH HAS NEVER WORKED IN A LIBREWOLF BUILD.  Push.kt looked up a string
#     resource named by R.string.pref_key_push_project_id -- whose value is the
#     literal "project_id" -- and returned a null PushConfig when it was
#     missing.  That resource comes from an XML credential file which
#     mobile/android/fenix/docs/Firebase-Cloud-Messaging-for-WebPush.md tells
#     developers to fetch from the Fenix team's Google Drive and drop into
#     fenix/app/src/debug/res/values/.  It is not in the tree, there is no
#     google-services.json, and the com.google.gms.google-services plugin is
#     not applied anywhere, so `pushConfig` was always null, `Push.feature` was
#     always null, and both `push.feature?.let { ... }` call sites were dead.
#     Confirmed on the running pre-patch build in logcat:
#       W PushConfig: No firebase configuration found; cannot support push service.
#     The FirebaseInitProvider, FirebaseMessagingService, InstanceIdReceiver and
#     the whole 459-class Firebase graph shipped anyway.
#   * PLAY INTEGRITY COULD NEVER GET A TOKEN.  Components.integrityClient
#     passed BuildConfig.GPS_INTEGRITY_TOKEN, which app/build.gradle fills from
#     ${rootDir}/.gps_integrity_token or leaves as "" -- and a LibreWolf tree
#     has no such file.  TokenProviderFactory.create() then returns a factory
#     that fails with InvalidProjectNumber and IntegrityManagerFactory is never
#     called.  The 54 integrity classes and their play-core support shipped
#     anyway.
#
#
# WHERE THE BOARD'S DESCRIPTION OF THIS TASK IS WRONG (checked, not assumed)
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The task text says Play Integrity is "used by the addon collection and
# account attestation" and that GMS provides "location services".  Neither is
# true of 153.0.4:
#
#   * ADD-ONS DO NOT TOUCH INTEGRITY.  `grep -rn -i integrity` over
#     android-components/components/feature/addons/src/main is empty, and
#     AddonCollectionProvider/AMOAddonsProvider have no attestation step.  The
#     only consumers of `Components.integrityClient` are Llm (the MLPA
#     summarisation proxy, via MlpaTokenProvider.mlpaIntegrityHandshake) and a
#     Secret-Settings debug-drawer screen.  So this patch does NOT change how
#     add-ons install, and LW-M3-07 (preinstall uBlock Origin) is unaffected --
#     that is a finding LW-M3-07 asked for.
#   * THERE IS NO GMS LOCATION PROVIDER TO REMOVE.  `play-services-location`,
#     `gms.location` and `FusedLocation` do not appear anywhere under
#     mobile/android, and no com/google/android/gms/location class is defined in
#     the pre-patch dex.  Geolocation.cpp:743 is an unconditional
#     `mProvider = new AndroidLocationProvider();` inside #ifdef
#     MOZ_WIDGET_ANDROID, so Gecko uses the platform LocationManager either way.
#     `:components:service-location` is Mozilla's own region lookup over HTTPS
#     and has no Google dependency.  Nothing here to do, and this is a checked
#     absence rather than an overlooked one.
#
#
# WHAT THIS COSTS -- STATE IT, DO NOT DISCOVER IT LATER
# ----------------------------------------------------
# 1. SYNC PUSH: GONE, AND SEND-TAB DEGRADES TO ON-DEMAND POLLING (not to a
#    timer).  FxaPushSupportFeature is no longer initialised, so this device
#    never registers an autopush subscription with FxA.  Incoming FxA device
#    commands -- "Send tab to device" and "Close tab on other device" -- are
#    delivered only when something calls
#    FxaDeviceConstellation.pollForCommands().  Because the current device's
#    `subscription` is now permanently null, refreshDevices()
#    (FxaDeviceConstellation.kt:240-246) always takes its
#    "needs push endpoint registration, so checking for missed commands" branch
#    and polls.  The reachable triggers, all of them in this tree:
#      - Account Settings -> "Sync Now"  (AccountSettingsFragment.syncNow()
#        calls refreshDevices() AND pollForCommands() explicitly)
#      - opening the synced-tabs screen  (DefaultController.refreshDevices())
#      - renaming the device            (FxaDeviceConstellation.kt:152)
#    The four-hourly PeriodicSyncConfig does NOT poll device commands: nothing
#    in the sync worker calls pollForCommands.  OUTGOING send-tab is unaffected
#    -- it is an HTTPS call to FxA -- so a LibreWolf phone can still send a tab
#    to a desktop instantly; it just will not receive one until it next syncs
#    or opens synced tabs.
# 2. WEB PUSH FOR WEBSITES: GONE.  PushProcessor is never installed and
#    WebPushEngineIntegration is deleted, so a site's
#    ServiceWorkerRegistration.pushManager.subscribe() fails.  It already
#    failed, for the reason above.
# 3. THE UI NO LONGER PROMISES PUSH.  The only push-shaped control in the app
#    was Secret Settings -> Sync Debug -> "Custom Push server"
#    (res/xml/sync_debug_preferences.xml + Settings.overridePushServer); it is
#    removed here, together with its preference key and its string.  A grep of
#    res/values/strings.xml finds no other user-facing string that promises
#    push delivery.
# 4. WEBAUTHN: PLATFORM-ONLY, SO ANDROID 14+ ONLY.  GeckoView implemented
#    WebAuthn on two backends and this patch removes one of them.  The platform
#    Credential Manager path (org.mozilla.gecko.WebAuthnCredentialManager, pure
#    android.credentials.*, no Google code) is untouched and still works on
#    API >= 34 when PackageManager.FEATURE_CREDENTIALS is present.  Below
#    Android 14, or on a 14+ device where the vendor disabled Credential Manager
#    (https://issuetracker.google.com/issues/349310440), WebAuthn now fails with
#    NOT_ALLOWED_ERR where it previously fell back to Play services FIDO2.  This
#    is a real capability loss on API 33 and older; there is no third backend --
#    AndroidWebAuthnService is the only WebAuthn transport Gecko compiles for
#    Android.  webAuthnIsUserVerifyingPlatformAuthenticatorAvailable() now
#    answers with exactly the gate WebAuthnCredentialManager.makeCredential()
#    itself applies, so it cannot claim a platform authenticator that would then
#    refuse.
# 5. IN-APP REVIEW: GONE.  PlayStoreReviewPromptController.tryPromptReview()
#    returns NotDisplayed instead of asking the Play Store to draw a rating
#    sheet.  Nothing dispatched that action anyway since LW-M4-10.  The "Rate on
#    Google Play" item in Settings still works -- it is a plain ACTION_VIEW
#    Intent with a web fallback and never used Play services.  Renaming or
#    removing that item is branding/strings work (LW-M4-07 / LW-M4-12), not
#    this patch.
# 6. GOOGLE ADVERTISING ID: GONE, and with it the AD_ID permission.
#    MetricsUtils.getAdvertisingID/getHashedIdentifier and ActivationPing are
#    deleted.  ActivationPing was already unreachable: its only caller was
#    GleanMetricsService, which LW-M4-01 deleted.
# 7. OSS-LICENSES: the com.google.android.gms:oss-licenses-plugin Gradle plugin
#    is no longer applied (it was applied whenever MOZILLA_OFFICIAL is set,
#    which it is in assets/mozconfig.android).  It generated the licence blob
#    for OssLicensesMenuActivity, which Fenix does not use -- Fenix's
#    "Open source libraries" screen is :components:support-license reading
#    licenses.json.  Nothing in the UI changes.
# 8. NO CHANGE TO GECKO.  This patch touches no C++, no JS and no
#    moz.build/moz.configure.  The three @WrapForJNI signatures in
#    WebAuthnTokenManager are byte-identical to upstream's, so the generated
#    WebAuthnTokenManagerWrappers.h/Natives.h and the three C++ files that use
#    them (dom/webauthn/AndroidWebAuthnService.cpp, PublicKeyCredential.cpp,
#    WebAuthnTransactionParent.cpp) are unchanged and libxul does not need
#    rebuilding.
#
#
