# THE TWO STRINGS THAT SURVIVE, AND WHY THEY ARE NOT A PLAY SERVICES DEPENDENCY
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Re-measured by LW-M4-16 on the combined build's APK
# (~/lw-batch-combined/apk/fenix-x86_64-debug.apk, 36 classes*.dex).  This
# replaces an earlier version of this section whose MECHANISM was wrong.  The
# conclusion is unchanged; the evidence for it is now much stronger.
#
# `./scripts/android-smoke.sh --check-no-gms` goes from 4,474 to **2**, not to
# zero, and this patch cannot take it to zero.  The two survivors are
#     com.google.android.gms.provider.action.PICK_IMAGES
#     com.google.android.gms.provider.extra.PICK_IMAGES_MAX
# and their exact identity in the artefact is
#     Landroidx/activity/result/contract/ActivityResultContracts$PickVisualMedia;
#         .GMS_ACTION_PICK_IMAGES       public static final String
#         .GMS_EXTRA_PICK_IMAGES_MAX    public static final String
# in androidx.activity 1.13.0 (gradle/libs.versions.toml:12), a PREBUILT Maven
# artifact.  In the dex they exist ONLY as that class's static_values encoded
# array -- the dex form of a .class ConstantValue attribute -- which is why they
# sit in classes.dex (the mergeExtDexDebug output, i.e. dependency code) and
# appear nowhere in the source tree.  Inside the AAR they are in exactly one
# class file, ActivityResultContracts$PickVisualMedia.class, and in nothing else
# the artifact ships (no manifest entry, no proguard.txt rule, no resource).
#
# THEY ARE INERT, AND THAT IS A MEASUREMENT, NOT AN INFERENCE.  Three facts,
# each read out of the built APK by walking the dex code items and decoding
# instruction widths, so a byte-pattern coincidence cannot fake a hit:
#   1. NO const-string / const-string/jumbo instruction in ANY of the 36 dex
#      files loads either literal.  Neither string can reach an Intent.
#   2. NO sget*/sput* instruction in ANY of the 36 dex files references either
#      field, and no dex other than classes.dex even carries a field_ids entry
#      for them.  Nothing reads the constants at runtime.
#   3. The fallback picker in 1.13.0 does NOT use the GMS action.  Its live
#      constant is a sibling field on the same class,
#        ACTION_SYSTEM_FALLBACK_PICK_IMAGES =
#            "androidx.activity.result.contract.action.PICK_IMAGES"
#      and that is what the three code sites load: PickVisualMedia.createIntent,
#      PickMultipleVisualMedia.createIntent, and
#      PickVisualMedia$Companion.getSystemFallbackPicker$activity, whose entire
#      body is
#        getPackageManager().resolveActivity(
#            new Intent("androidx.activity.result.contract.action.PICK_IMAGES"),
#            MATCH_DEFAULT_ONLY|MATCH_SYSTEM_ONLY)
#      (javap of the AAR's classes.jar).  AndroidX moved this action off the
#      Play services name onto a vendor-neutral one; the GMS_* pair is retained
#      only as source/binary-compatible public API for callers that named it.
#      An earlier version of this header said the backport "resolves that
#      implicit Intent action" -- true of activity 1.7-1.9, FALSE of 1.13.0, and
#      the correction matters because the real answer is stronger: the string is
#      not merely unresolvable on a GMS-free device, it is never even loaded.
#   The class itself IS used -- android-components
#   feature/prompts/.../AndroidPhotoPicker.kt (the `<input type=file>` picker)
#   and fenix .../components/lens/LensCameraActivity.kt -- and its
#   isPhotoPickerAvailable(context) resolves to isSystemPickerAvailable(), an
#   SDK-version test.  Using the class does not read the GMS fields.
#   Also measured: the same two strings, equally unreferenced, are present in
#   the PRE-patch APK (~/lw-m2-04/out-make/apk/fenix-x86_64-debug.apk).  They
#   are not residue of the Play services removal.  They were never a Play
#   services dependency in the first place.
#
# WHY THEY ARE NOT REMOVED, AND WHY BOTH WAYS TO REMOVE THEM WERE REJECTED
#   * Vendoring a forked androidx.activity: an AndroidX core artifact, forked to
#     delete two unread constants.  Rebase cost every release, zero behaviour
#     change.
#   * An AGP Instrumentation / ASM class transform over InstrumentationScope.ALL
#     that strips the constants out of the dependency's bytecode.  This is the
#     tempting one and it is worse than doing nothing: it would erase the
#     strings without changing a single instruction, and it would install a
#     mechanism that ALSO hides a real GMS reintroduction from the very gate
#     that exists to catch one.  A later rebase that pulled play-services back
#     in transitively would come back clean.
#   R8 is not an option either: minifyEnabled is false for the debug variant the
#   harness must use (it needs a debuggable APK), and basing the gate on a
#   minified APK would WEAKEN it, because R8 renames and prunes real GMS code
#   too.
#
# WHAT THE CHECK MUST DO INSTEAD -- AND IT IS NOT A THRESHOLD OF 2
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# LW-M4-16 does not own scripts/android-smoke.sh, so the contract change is a
# hand-off to LW-M2-07.  `--check-no-gms` should require ZERO of everything that
# can execute or be resolved -- Google-prefixed classes DEFINED, Google-prefixed
# type/method/field REFERENCES, gms|firebase|play-services APK entries, and any
# GMS literal LOADED by a const-string instruction -- and exempt exactly these
# two literals BY FIELD NAME, re-proving on every run that each occurs only as
# that field's initialiser, that no instruction loads it, and that no sget/sput
# reads it.  A GMS literal that is not one of the two named pairs is then a hard
# failure at count 1, and so is either of them acquiring a reader.  That check
# was written, wired into --self-test, and FALSIFIED FIVE WAYS through the real
# harness before this paragraph was: the full-GMS pre-patch APK, the exemption's
# expected value made wrong, its expected field name made wrong, a synthetic dex
# with one exempt literal's text altered, and a synthetic dex with an existing
# sget-object repointed at GMS_ACTION_PICK_IMAGES.  All five exit 1; the
# unmodified combined APK exits 0.  The hand-off is a ready-to-apply patch,
# /home/mgysin/lw-m4-16/android-smoke-no-gms.diff on the reference host; see the
# SECOND ADDENDUM at the end of this header for its re-verification.
#
# The measurements that DID reach zero, and that are what "zero GMS
# dependencies" means -- all re-measured by LW-M4-16 on the combined APK:
#   0 classes DEFINED under Lcom/google/android/gms/, Lcom/google/firebase/,
#     Lcom/google/android/play/ or Lcom/google/android/datatransport/ -- 2,935
#     before.  Lcom/google/mlkit/ is also 0, and was 0 before as well: see
#     "WHAT DELIBERATELY STAYS" above, it is a checked absence not a removal.
#   0 type_ids, 0 method_ids and 0 field_ids naming any of those prefixes
#     (3,075 type refs and 21,006 member refs before) -- a reference the runtime
#     would have to resolve is a dependency even when no class is present
#   0 google/firebase entities in the merged AndroidManifest.xml (26 before);
#     `strings -el` over the binary manifest and over resources.arsc is empty
#   0 APK entries whose NAME matches gms|firebase|play-services (14 before on
#     that needle set, which is wider than the 6 counted higher up because it
#     also catches e.g. META-INF/kotlinx_coroutines_play_services.version),
#     and 0 native libraries
#   0 GMS literals LOADED by any instruction (197 before, among them Fenix's own
#     ShareToAppsSafeExtras telemetry allow-list, removed by this patch)
#
#
# HOW THIS WAS VERIFIED
# ---------------------
# Built through scripts/android-apk.sh --skip-gecko (Gradle stage only, reusing
# the objdir and the fat AAR -- this patch changes no Gecko input), then:
#   * DEX class_defs/type_ids over all 36 classes*.dex of the built APK:
#     63,646 defined classes, of which ZERO under com.google.android.gms,
#     com.google.firebase, com.google.android.play or com.google.mlkit
#     (2,623 before).  `--check-no-gms`: 4,474 -> 2, see above.
#   * `aapt2 dump xmltree --file AndroidManifest.xml` on the built APK: not one
#     line matching gms|firebase|c2dm|com.google remains, from 26 entities.
#   * `mach gradle fenix:compileDebugUnitTestKotlin
#      geckoview:compileDebugUnitTestJavaWithJavac` exits 0 -- the test edits in
#     this patch compile (Kotlin warnings are errors in this build:
#     ProjectPlugin.kt:229-242 sets allWarningsAsErrors on every KotlinCompile).
#   * the full baseline smoke suite on a headless x86_64 emulator running the
#     android-30 `default` system image -- NO Google APIs, PlayStore.enabled
#     false, `pm list packages` matching gms|google|vending|gsf returns nothing.
#     All 7 checks pass: page-load http and https, webgl, video, getusermedia,
